@page
@model AzureModel
@using PrototypeManager.Web.Pages.Guidance
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Azure hosting";
    ViewData[GuidanceNavigation.SectionViewDataKey] = GuidanceNavigation.TechnicalAzure;
}

@section SideNav {
    @await Html.PartialAsync("_GuidanceSideNav")
}

<div class="dfe-c-fe-shell">
    <header class="dfe-c-fe-page-header">
        <div class="dfe-c-fe-page-header__intro">
            <p class="dfe-c-fe-eyebrow">Technical documentation</p>
            <h1 class="dfe-c-fe-title">Azure hosting</h1>
            <p class="dfe-c-fe-text govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">
                Each prototype gets its own resource group and Linux Node web app, attached to a shared Free App Service plan pool.
            </p>
        </div>
    </header>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">What gets created</h2>
    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>a dedicated resource group per prototype (naming prefix <code>s186d01-pt-</code>)</li>
        <li>a Linux web app running Node (<code>NODE|24-lts</code>), HTTPS only, FTPS disabled</li>
        <li>the web app is attached to an existing Free (F1) App Service plan — not a new plan per prototype</li>
        <li>standard tags for Environment, Product and Service Offering</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="govuk-body">
        Infrastructure is defined in Bicep, compiled to ARM JSON, and deployed with the Azure SDK (not the Azure CLI).
        Admins can check subscription access, the Free plan pool, and GitHub on
        <a class="govuk-link" href="@Url.Page("/Admin/DependencyHealth")">Dependency health</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m govuk-!-margin-top-6">Free App Service plan pool</h2>
    <p class="govuk-body">
        Azure limits how many Free plans and how many apps per Free plan you can have in a region.
        Prototype Manager keeps a shared pool of Free plans in a dedicated resource group and assigns new web apps into a plan that still has capacity.
    </p>
    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>shared plans resource group (for example <code>s186d01-pt-rg-plans</code>)</li>
        <li>up to 10 Free plans, up to 10 apps per plan (region quota-aware)</li>
        <li>deleting a prototype removes its resource group and web app, but leaves empty pool plans in place for reuse</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m govuk-!-margin-top-6">Temporary higher SKUs</h2>
    <p class="govuk-body">
        For short research spikes, Admin can escalate a prototype to a dedicated B1 or B2 plan inside the prototype resource group.
        When the temporary window expires, a background process moves the app back onto the Free pool.
    </p>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m govuk-!-margin-top-6">Cost controls</h2>
    <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>allowed region typically West Europe</li>
        <li>default allowed SKU F1</li>
        <li>maximum expiry days enforced in policy</li>
        <li>users confirm no real user data and not-production use</li>
    </ul>
</div>
